      `Japan suits programmatic SEO unusually well. People search by station, line, ward and city, the country has well over a thousand municipalities, and many industries have structured data that maps neatly onto those places. A property company, a recruitment business or a home service provider can serve real demand with thousands of pages, if each page is genuinely useful.`,
      `Typical structures we build include property pages by prefecture, city, station and property type; service pages by city for moving, cleaning, repairs or legal services; job listings by prefecture and occupation; B2B pages by material, process and industry; and tourism pages by area and season. Our SEO website plan starts from ${both("SEO website")} for 700+ pages, with the data pipeline built so new records create new pages automatically. When the data lives in an existing business system, the integration work is the kind of project described on our <a href="/japan/software-development/">software development page for Japan</a>.`,
      `The risk is well known. Pages that differ only by a place name are thin content, and Google's spam policies name scaled content abuse, meaning large numbers of pages produced mainly to manipulate rankings, as a violation. Our safeguards:`,
